<title>BELGIUM: Belgium wants Telecoms Council to discuss child-sex porn.</title>
<headline>Belgium wants Telecoms Council to discuss child-sex porn.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian Telecommunications Minister Elio di Rupo said on Thursday he wanted the September 27 Telecommunications Council to discuss ways to keep child-sex pornography off the Internet.</p>
<p>He said he had asked the Irish presidency to place the item on the agenda.</p>
<p>&quot;Given the extreme complexity of the problem, Elio Di Rupo is convinced that a solution at least at European level must be considered in all urgency,&quot; his office said in a statement.</p>
<p>He said he had already won support from French Telecommunications Minister Francois Fillon during a meeting on Thursday.</p>
</text>
